            "body": "Yes, it is. `buf_write` calls `buf_write_do_autocmds` [[1]](https://github.com/dmitmel/neovim/blob/8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff/src/nvim/bufwrite.c#L1065-L1067), which calls `apply_autocmds_exarg` with `EVENT_BUFWRITECMD` [[2]](https://github.com/dmitmel/neovim/blob/8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff/src/nvim/bufwrite.c#L394) and the short file name (`sfname`) as the argument, which in turn calls `apply_autocmds_group` [[3]](https://github.com/dmitmel/neovim/blob/8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff/src/nvim/autocmd.c#L1633), which saves the argument it was called with into `autocmd_fname` [[4]](https://github.com/dmitmel/neovim/blob/8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff/src/nvim/autocmd.c#L1790-L1814), which is keeps the value of `<afile>`, then it expands this argument into an absolute path if the requested autocmd is not part of the list of autocmds which don't take a file argument [[5]](https://github.com/dmitmel/neovim/blob/8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff/src/nvim/autocmd.c#L1842-L1879), AND THEN that fully expanded path is assigned to `autocmd_match` [[6]](https://github.com/dmitmel/neovim/blob/8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff/src/nvim/autocmd.c#L1903-L1904), which stores the value of `<amatch>`. So yes, `<amatch>` is guaranteed to be an absolute path.",
            "commit_id": "8254e1ef4e55a5ff1f3e11d876c4e80301fa6cff",
            "created_at": "2026-06-27T11:38:44Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -54,7 +54,12 @@ def_autocmd('BufWriteCmd', {}, function(ev)\n   local buflines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, 0, -1, false)\n   local ret = vim.fn.writefile(shada_get_binstrings(buflines), ev.file, 'b')\n   if ret == 0 then\n-    vim.bo[ev.buf].modified = false\n+    -- To check that we are not saving into a different file, we must compare ev.match (always an\n+    -- absolute path), and not ev.file (can be relative), against nvim_buf_get_name() (always\n+    -- returns an absolute path).\n+    if ev.match == vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(ev.buf) or vim.o.cpoptions:find('%+') then",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40412#discussion_r3485939163",
            "id": 3485939163,
